  <!-- ══ DAY 1 ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="day-block" id="day1">
    <div class="day-header">Day 1</div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~10 miles from Sunriver — drive only -->
    <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚕  12 min → Lava Butte</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Lava Butte | Type 2 self · 500-ft cinder cone with summit road · qualifying nature stop · 4.6★ AllTrails · Wikipedia -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">1.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Lava Butte</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 A 500-foot red cinder cone that erupted about 7000 years ago, ringed by the black basalt of the Lava Lands flow. A road spirals to the rim, where a lookout tower and crater trail open onto a sweep of Cascade peaks and the high-desert lava plain below.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_Butte" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Daily 9:00am - 5:00pm</div>
        <div>⏰ ~1.5 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ The visitor center and summit road open May 15 through September 15 only.</div>
        <div>⚠️ Mid-June to early September the summit road is reached by shuttle from Lava Lands Visitor Center only — private vehicles are turned back during shuttle hours.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lava+Lands+Visitor+Center+58201+S+Hwy+97+Bend+OR+97707" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lava Lands Visitor Center · 58201 S Hwy 97</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Lava_Butte_and_Newberry_1.jpg" alt="Lava Butte"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~2 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  5 min → Lava River Cave</div>

    <!-- tour-search: Lava River Cave guided tours Bend Oregon — self-guided timed-entry only via recreation.gov; the guided lava-cave tour is a different cave network (Wanderlust), shipped in Tours -->
    <!-- inclusion-bar: Lava River Cave | Type 2 self ticket-gated · Oregon's longest lava tube · qualifying cave stop · 4.6★ recreation.gov -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">2.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Lava River Cave</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 Oregon's longest lava tube at nearly one mile, carved by basalt flows over 80000 years ago. Walk through towering chambers and constricted passages with a rented lantern — a self-guided underground stretch that stays a steady 42 degrees no matter the season above.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_River_Cave" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="ticket-box">
        <div>🎟️ <a href="https://www.recreation.gov/timed-entry/10089508" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Timed-Entry Ticket 4.6⭐</strong> · recreation.gov</a></div>
        <div>🏛️ Daily 9:00am - 5:00pm</div>
        <div>⏰ ~1.5 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ Open for the season May through September only.</div>
        <div>⚠️ Timed-entry tickets sell out 2 - 3 weeks ahead in summer — book before your trip. No walk-up when sold out.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lava+River+Cave+Bend+OR+97707" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lava River Cave · S Hwy 97</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Lava_river_cave_oregon.jpg" alt="Lava River Cave"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~30 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  45 min → Paulina Falls</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Paulina Falls | Type 2 self · twin 80-ft waterfall in Newberry Caldera · qualifying nature stop · 4.7★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">3.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Paulina Falls</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 A twin 80-foot waterfall where Paulina Creek pours over the rim of the Newberry Caldera. A short trail leads to an overlook at the lip and a second viewpoint at the base, where the two ribbons drop side by side into a rust-and-grey rock amphitheatre.</div>
      <!-- no-wikipedia: no standalone English Wikipedia article — covered only within Newberry Volcano -->

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
        <div>⏰ ~45 min</div>
        <div>⚠️ Paulina Lake Road closes mid-November through late May under snow — the caldera is reachable only in the warm months.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Paulina+Falls+Newberry+National+Volcanic+Monument+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paulina Falls · Paulina Lake Rd</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Paulina_Falls,_Oregon_(2014)_-_01.JPG" alt="Paulina Falls"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~11 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  20 min → Big Obsidian Flow</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Big Obsidian Flow | Type 2 self · 1300-year-old obsidian and pumice flow · qualifying nature stop · 766 reviews AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">4.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Big Obsidian Flow</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 Oregon's youngest lava flow — about 1300 years old — a glittering mile-wide field of black volcanic glass and chalk-white pumice inside the Newberry Caldera. A one-mile interpretive loop climbs onto the flow itself, with Paulina and East Lakes spreading out below.</div>
      <!-- no-wikipedia: no standalone English Wikipedia article — covered only within Newberry Volcano -->

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
        <div>⏰ ~1 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ The trail climbs onto loose obsidian and pumice — stay on the path, and skip it in rain or snow when the glass turns slick.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Big+Obsidian+Flow+Trailhead+Newberry+National+Volcanic+Monument+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Big Obsidian Flow Trailhead · Paulina Lake Rd</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Big_Obsidian_Flow_8277.jpg" alt="Big Obsidian Flow"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~35 miles to hotel — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  55 min → hotel</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ DAY 2 ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="day-block" id="day2">
    <div class="day-header">Day 2</div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~31 miles from Sunriver — drive only -->
    <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚕  40 min → Smith Rock State Park</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Smith Rock State Park | Type 2 self · world-class basalt canyon · qualifying nature stop · 4.8★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">1.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Smith Rock State Park</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 World-class basalt formations rising 650 ft above the Crooked River gorge. The 3.4-mile River Trail loops through cathedral spires, past Monkey Face column and Morning Glory Wall, with sweeping canyon views the entire way.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smith_Rock_State_Park" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Daily 6:00am - 10:00pm</div>
        <div>⏰ ~3 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ Parking fills by 9:00am on summer weekends — arrive early or use the overflow lot north of the park.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=9241+NE+Crooked+River+Dr%2C+Terrebonne%2C+OR+97760" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">9241 NE Crooked River Dr · Terrebonne</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos">
        <img src="_build/assets/800px-Smith_Rock_State_Park_Oregon.jpg" alt="Smith Rock State Park">
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~3 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  8 min → Peter Skene Ogden Viewpoint</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Peter Skene Ogden State Scenic Viewpoint | Type 2 self · 300-ft Crooked River canyon overlook · qualifying nature viewpoint · Lonely Planet · Wikipedia -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">2.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Peter Skene Ogden Viewpoint</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 At Peter Skene Ogden State Scenic Viewpoint the Crooked River cuts a sheer 300-foot slot through the basalt, spanned by three historic bridges side by side. A short cliffside path runs to railed overlooks straight down into the gorge — dramatic and reached in minutes from the car.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Skene_Ogden_State_Scenic_Viewpoint" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
        <div>⏰ ~30 min</div>
        <div>⚠️ The rim is unfenced beyond the developed overlooks — the drop is sheer 300 feet, so keep back from the edge.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Peter+Skene+Ogden+State+Scenic+Viewpoint+US-97+Terrebonne+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Peter Skene Ogden Viewpoint · US-97 · Terrebonne</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Crooked_River_through_gorge.jpg" alt="Crooked River Gorge"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~17 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  25 min → Pilot Butte State Scenic Viewpoint</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Pilot Butte State Scenic Viewpoint | Type 2 self · 360° Cascade panorama · qualifying nature viewpoint · 4.7★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">3.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Pilot Butte State Scenic Viewpoint</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 An extinct cinder cone rising 500 feet above Bend, offering an uninterrupted 360° panorama of nine Cascade peaks — Mt. Bachelor, South Sister, Broken Top, Mt. Jefferson, and more. Drive or hike the paved 1-mile summit trail.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilot_Butte_(Oregon)" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Daily 6:00am - 10:00pm</div>
        <div>⏰ ~45 min</div>
        <div>🆓 Free</div>
        <div>⚠️ Summit road closed November through April.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=1310+NE+Hwy+20%2C+Bend%2C+OR+97701" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">1310 NE Hwy 20</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-View_from_Pilot_Butte_Park_Bend_Oregon_2013.jpg" alt="View from Pilot Butte State Scenic Viewpoint"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~23 miles to hotel — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  22 min → hotel</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ DAY 3 ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="day-block" id="day3">
    <div class="day-header">Day 3</div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~26 miles from Sunriver — drive only -->
    <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚕  38 min → Tumalo Falls</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Tumalo Falls | Type 2 self · 97-foot waterfall · qualifying nature stop · 4.8★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">1.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Tumalo Falls</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 A 97-foot ribbon of water plunging into a narrow basalt canyon, reached by a 3.4-mile round-trip trail through ponderosa pines along Tumalo Creek. One of the most dramatic single-drop waterfalls in Central Oregon.</div>
      <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumalo_Falls" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikipedia</a></div>

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Daily 8:00am - 8:00pm</div>
        <div>⏰ ~2.5 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ Road closed November through May.</div>
        <div>⚠️ Parking lot fills by 9:00am on summer weekends — arrive before 8:30am or after 3:00pm.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tumalo+Falls+Day+Use+Area%2C+Skyliners+Rd%2C+Bend%2C+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tumalo Falls Day Use Area · Skyliners Rd</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Tumalo_Falls_Waterfalls_Oregon.jpg" alt="Tumalo Falls"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~33 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  50 min → Sparks Lake</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Sparks Lake | Type 2 self · iconic Mt Bachelor reflection lake · qualifying nature stop · 4.7★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">2.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Sparks Lake</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 A shallow lava-dammed lake on the Cascade Lakes Scenic Byway, ringed by marsh and black lava and backed by Mt. Bachelor and South Sister. The mirror-still water at first light is the scene photographer Ray Atkeson made famous — the 2.5-mile shoreline loop hugs the view.</div>
      <!-- no-wikipedia: no substantive standalone English Wikipedia article -->

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
        <div>⏰ ~1.5 hr</div>
        <div>⚠️ The Cascade Lakes Highway closes under snow late November through late May, and the gravel access road is rough for low-clearance cars in early summer.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sparks+Lake+Day+Use+Area+Cascade+Lakes+Highway+Bend+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sparks Lake Day Use · Cascade Lakes Hwy</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Sparks_Lake,_Oregon_(2012)_-_01.jpg" alt="Sparks Lake"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~5 miles between stops — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  8 min → Devils Lake</div>

    <!-- inclusion-bar: Devils Lake | Type 2 self · glacial turquoise lake on the Cascade Lakes Byway · qualifying nature stop · 4.6★ AllTrails -->
    <div class="stop-block">
      <div class="stop-header">
        <span class="stop-num">3.</span>
        <span class="stop-name self">Devils Lake</span>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-row">📒 A tiny glacier-fed lake so clear and shallow it glows an unreal Caribbean turquoise over its white pumice bed. A few steps from the byway pullout deliver the whole scene — float, wade, or just stand at the shore and take in one of the most startling colors in the Cascades.</div>
      <!-- no-wikipedia: no substantive standalone English Wikipedia article -->

      <div class="tour-box">
        <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
        <div>⏰ ~45 min</div>
        <div>⚠️ On the Cascade Lakes Highway — closed under snow late November through late May along with the rest of the byway.</div>
        <div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Devils+Lake+Cascade+Lakes+Highway+Bend+OR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Devils Lake · Cascade Lakes Hwy</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stop-photos"><img src="_build/assets/800px-Devils_Lake,_Oregon_-_Flickr_-_Bonnie_Moreland_(free_images).jpg" alt="Devils Lake"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- walk-over-40: ~33 miles to hotel — drive only -->
    <div class="next">🚕  50 min → hotel</div>
  </div>

