  <!-- ══ CLAUDE INSPIRATION ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="claude-inspiration theme-yellow" id="claude-inspiration">
    <div class="extras-title">🌋 High Desert Light</div>
    <p>Bend sits at 3600 feet in the rain shadow of the Cascades — a place where the light is different from anywhere else in Oregon. The high desert air is dry enough that mornings have an alpine clarity and evenings turn the rimrock orange-gold. Most places with this quality of light are either inaccessible or exhausting to reach. Here, you drive 20 minutes from the courts to a world-class canyon, spend the day in it, and drive home.</p>
    <p>The trip is built on one logic: play hard, then go somewhere genuinely spectacular for a few hours. The whole region is volcanic — Lava Butte and the Newberry Caldera south of the house, Smith Rock's basalt spires to the north, the Cascade Lakes glittering to the west. You are never circling the same scenery twice, and you are never more than an hour from the door.</p>
  </div>

